caption: Gift Manifestation
tradition-component: gift-manifestation

A Dreadhound may also configure a Super-Memorization slot from any Gift in their Eldritch Core, whether Latent or Realized, even when they have no Current Prey, Psychic Pattern, or Prey Repository. The loaded trait must be a legal, mechanically defensible expression of that Gift and represents temporarily expressing that part of the Eldritch pattern. A Gift-derived configuration does not require a governing Psi Talent and does not take Only Against Current Prey, -20%. It is not limited by Gift Value; its point value is limited only by the Dreadhound's available Super-Memorization capacity and all other applicable caps and construction rules. A Realized Gift may serve as this Dreadhound repository even though Realized Gifts are not normal Eldritch Core Power Stunt sources; this is a specific Dreadhound exception and does not make the Gift Latent again or alter any permanent ability that Realized it. A given Gift may occupy no more than one Super-Memorization slot at a time, even if additional proposed manifestations of that Gift would be mechanically or conceptually divergent. Before Mastery a Gift-derived configuration may use Advanced construction; after Mastery it may use Master construction where appropriate. Loading a Gift-derived trait does not by itself Realize a Latent Gift or grant permanent purchase permission.
